cadtui localisation — CAD command-name probe via getcname (P2, CI/runner)

Parent: cadtui.issue (Phase 7). Harvest the localised CAD COMMAND NAMES that
cadtui's local-name/international-name need. This CANNOT be produced headless —
it must be measured on localised AutoCAD/BricsCAD installs.

What to collect
- For each command in the command set, call getcname BOTH directions:
  local -> _INTERNATIONAL and international -> local (spec lines ~122-140,
  ~750-756). getcname output is generated fact and safe to import.
- On BricsCAD also capture the COMMANDS listing (English + localised).

How (mirror the alfe CAD probe pattern already in the repo)
- A probe .lsp under probes/sources/ driven by alfe against the real CAD,
  registered in probes/sources/manifest.txt.
- New SOFT, cad-tagged jobs in .gitlab/native.yml (extend
  .gate-windows-cad-soft / .gate-macos-cad-soft) — soft because a probe measures,
  it must never gate a release. Emit artifacts under dist/getcname/.
- Localised installs (one per target locale) are a runner-provisioning concern
  (pjb), like BRICSCAD_PROFILE_CLEAN for the sysvar harvest. See memory
  "alfe CAD probe jobs" (ogamita/rules alfe-cad-probe-rules.md) — BricsCAD is
  GREEN on both macOS+Windows; AutoCAD on Windows.

Matrix
- BricsCAD on macOS AND Windows (a divergence is itself an answer), AutoCAD on
  Windows. One run per locale (fr_FR first).

Output feeds cadtui-locale-data-format-and-loader.issue (commands.sexp via the
converter). Missing entries fall back to the international form.


Resolved (2026-10-26, clautolisp 2.3.69, MR !494)
-------------------------------------------------

fr_FR is harvested on the whole matrix: BricsCAD macOS and AutoCAD Windows
since 2026-09-13/14 (cadtui's fr_FR/command.sexp, 118 commands), BricsCAD V25
Windows, AutoCAD 2022 and AcCoreConsole on 2026-10-26 (jobs 17460836643,
17460836644, 17460836645).

The probe gained a GETCNAME-EDGE section (no underscore, case, the - ' .
prefixes, accents, unknown names, a user C: command, non-strings). What it
measured is in the spec's GETCNAME entry ("Measured"); the gist: a leading
_ asks for the local name, anything else is a local name; AutoCAD also
strips . and ' and ignores accents, BricsCAD does neither; each product
knows its own command set.

clautolisp's GETCNAME was a nil stub; it is now real (2.3.69): HOST-GETCNAME,
cador's CADOR-GETCNAME over per-product tables (cador/data/getcname/
fr_FR.sexp, made by scripts/getcname-to-cador.py from the reports, the
identity commands kept), the BricsCAD dialects with BricsCAD's rules, the
others AutoCAD's, in the session's language; under English a command is its
own local name. Tests GETCNAME-FOLLOWS-EACH-PRODUCT-UNDER-FR-FR (every
measured row, both products), GETCNAME-UNDER-A-LOCALE-WITHOUT-A-TABLE-IS-
THE-IDENTITY, GETCNAME-BUILTIN-TAKES-A-STRING.

Left (needs localised CAD installs on the runners, pjb):
issues/open/deferred-getcname-other-locales.issue.
